From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:36:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 257/342] realtekwifi: RTL8822BU, phase 2 (association and
 WPA2)

Station mode for the RTL8822BU: media status and default port H2C on
association, firmware rate adaptation (RA info, RSSI monitor, the
firmware's rate reports shown as the node's Tx rate), management and
EAPOL frames at fixed low rates, IQK once per channel (at join, not
while scanning) and again on a temperature change of 8 or more,
hardware crypto for pairwise and group keys with rtw88's CAM group bit,
frames the hardware left encrypted handed to net80211, and the AID,
RRSR, preamble and basic rate registers as rtw88 leaves them. From
rtw88 (v7.0) under BSD-3-Clause, as phase 1.

rtwn core: cam_group_bits, 0 on every other chip.

Compile-tested only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
